.TH SSH-GATE 1 "November 2026" "ssh-gate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ssh-gate \- SOCKS5 and HTTP proxy over SSH server pools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssh-gate
.RB [ --config
.IR file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I ssh-gate
serves SOCKS5 and HTTP CONNECT proxies. It assigns each new tunnel to one
eligible SSH server using rendezvous hashing over the client IP and the
destination. An established connection stays on its selected SSH transport
until it closes. Direct rules bypass SSH and remain available while all SSH
servers are down.
.PP
Each configured server has its own pool of SSH transports, health state,
tunnel quota and pending-open quotas. A shared HTTPS URL is checked through
each server with certificate verification. Hostname resolution for tunnel
destinations uses DNS over the selected SSH server and does not fall back to
local DNS.
.PP
The Ed25519 client key is generated on first start. Add its public key to the
SSH account's
.IR authorized_keys .
SSH host fingerprints are pinned by server ID in
.IR ssh_known_hosts .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --config " file"
Read the strict YAML configuration from
.IR file .
Default:
.IR /etc/ssh-gate/config.yaml .
Configuration changes take effect after restart. Unknown fields and invalid
values prevent startup.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The root keys are
.BR proxy ,
.BR routing ,
.BR ssh ,
.BR balancing ,
.BR dns ,
.BR health ,
.BR ui ,
.BR logging ,
and
.BR storage .
See
.I /usr/share/doc/ssh-gate/config.example.yaml
for a complete example.
.TP
.B proxy.socks5.listen, proxy.http.listen
Lists of listen addresses. Presence of each section enables that proxy.
.TP
.B routing.direct.rules
Ordered domain, regular-expression and
.B ip:
CIDR rules for local direct routing. Domain and regex rules use the local
resolver. Matching CIDRs can use tunnel DNS to decide the route, then resolve
locally for the direct connection. Accepts a YAML sequence, or one
comma-separated string in the form the old
.B DIRECT_RULES
variable held; only the string form splits entries on commas.
.TP
.B ssh.servers[]
Each entry has a stable
.BR id ,
.BR host ,
.BR port ,
.BR user ,
optional
.B transports
and optional per-server
.BR limits .
Defaults are four SSH transports, 4096 client tunnels, 256 pending client
opens and 32 pending service opens. All servers use the one generated client
key. A legacy single fingerprint in
.I ssh_known_hosts
must be explicitly assigned to one server ID.
.TP
.B balancing.hash_key
Either
.B client_ip_destination
(default) or
.BR client_ip .
Source and destination ports are not part of the hash.
.TP
.B balancing.retry
Maximum channel-open attempts (default 3) and the total time budget
(default 30s).
.TP
.B balancing.passive
Per-server failure threshold and exclusion interval. Defaults: three
confirmed transport failures within 30s, excluded for 30s.
.TP
.B dns.tunnel.servers, dns.tunnel.doh_host
Tunnel DNS servers or one DNS-over-HTTPS hostname. These forms are mutually
exclusive. A tunnel route never falls back to local DNS, including after
NXDOMAIN.
.TP
.B health.url, health.interval, health.timeout, health.max_fails, health.successes
Common HTTPS probe settings. Defaults are
.B https://www.youtube.com
, 10s, 5s, three failures and two successes. TLS is verified, redirects are
not followed, and every probe uses a fresh SSH channel and a fresh DNS lookup.
.TP
.B storage.directory
Directory for the generated key pair and host key pins. The Debian unit uses
.IR /var/lib/ssh-gate .
.SH HEALTH AND STATUS
.TP
.B /healthz
Liveness endpoint.
.TP
.B /readyz
Returns success when configured proxy listeners are running. Readiness does
not depend on SSH pool health, allowing direct routes to continue during an
SSH outage.
.TP
.B /api/status
Returns aggregate SSH connectivity and eligibility plus a
.B ssh.servers[]
entry for each server. Server status includes health, reasons, channel and
quota use, and transport states with TCP statistics when available. The
response also includes DNS status, active connection counts and uptime.
.TP
.B /api/connections
Lists active and completed tunneled client connections, including selected
server ID and transport slot.
.PP
The Web UI is served from
.BR / .
The UI and API accept only loopback/allowed Host names and have no
authentication. Keep the health listener on a trusted interface.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ssh-gate/config.yaml
System configuration, supplied as a package conffile.
.TP
.I /var/lib/ssh-gate/ssh_key
Private Ed25519 client key.
.TP
.I /var/lib/ssh-gate/ssh_key.pub
Public client key to install in
.IR authorized_keys .
.TP
.I /var/lib/ssh-gate/ssh_known_hosts
Host key fingerprints indexed by server ID.
.SH MIGRATION
The old
.I /etc/default/ssh-gate
environment file is no longer read. Copy its values into the nested YAML
schema; one old SSH endpoint becomes one item under
.BR ssh.servers .
The old application-wide
.B MAX_CONNECTIONS
becomes per-server
.BR ssh.servers[].limits.max_client_tunnels .
There is no local DNS fallback on tunnel NXDOMAIN. Preserve the old
single-line host fingerprint and convert it explicitly to
.BR "server-id SHA256:fingerprint" .
The generated client key remains usable. Before rollback, restore the old
configuration and original one-line host pin together with the old binary.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal shutdown.
.TP
.B 78
Invalid configuration or another startup error that will not be fixed by
restarting, such as a busy listen address or unreadable key.
.SH EXAMPLES
Copy and edit the complete sample:
.P
.EX
cp /usr/share/doc/ssh-gate/config.example.yaml /etc/ssh-gate/config.yaml
sudoedit /etc/ssh-gate/config.yaml
systemctl restart ssh-gate
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR sshd (8),
.BR sshd_config (5)
